        "answer": {
          "short": "The three branches join continuously at the included points $(0,1)$ and $(1,1)$.",
          "worked": "At the break points,\n$$\\begin{align*}f_L(0)&=-0+1\\\\f_L(0)&=1\\\\f(0)&=1\\\\f_L(1)&=1\\\\f(1)&=2(1)-1\\\\f(1)&=1\\end{align*}$$\nPlot $y=-x+1$ only for $x<0$, $y=1$ for $0\\le x<1$, and $y=2x-1$ for $x\\ge1$. Both joins, $(0,1)$ and $(1,1)$, are included, so there are no holes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
